    rk_why_title: 'Why it matters, in plain words',
    rk_why_cm_fs: 'If the factory’s food-safety certificate has run out, a recall or a fine can land on your brand, because your name is on the label.',
    rk_why_cm_ip: 'Nothing stops the factory from reusing your recipe or making it for someone else.',
    rk_why_cm_recall: 'If a batch goes bad, nobody has agreed who takes it off the shelves or who pays, so you argue while it is still on sale.',
    rk_why_da_credit: 'If the distributor stops paying, you may never get your money back, because the credit you give them is not backed by a bank guarantee.',
    rk_why_da_excl: 'It is unclear whether the distributor has the area to themselves, which causes fights when another seller moves in.',
    rk_why_da_perf: 'A distributor who sells too little can keep the area for good, because you cannot end the deal for poor sales.',
    rk_why_eq_credit: 'If the machine breaks down you get nothing back, even though the downtime stops your sales.',
    rk_why_eq_eq: 'The contract does not say which machine it covers, so it is unclear what is being leased, insured or serviced.',
    rk_why_eq_title: 'If the leasing company goes bust, you could lose the machine your production depends on.',
    rk_why_ff_ins: 'If goods are stolen or damaged on the road, there may be no insurance to pay for them, only an argument over who is to blame.',
    rk_why_ff_otif: 'Late or short deliveries cost the carrier nothing, so there is little to make them improve.',
    rk_why_ff_reg: 'The delivery routes are not named, so prices, delivery times and service targets are open to argument.',
    rk_why_le_dep: 'No deposit is set, so you have nothing to fall back on if rent goes unpaid or the property is damaged.',
    rk_why_le_esc: 'The rent stays the same for the whole lease, so one side loses out as prices rise and pressure builds to renegotiate.',
    rk_why_le_stamp: 'Nothing shows the tax on this lease was paid, which can make the lease hard to rely on and bring penalties.',
    rk_why_mk_appr: 'No spending limit is set, so either every small cost needs sign-off or big costs slip through unchecked.',
    rk_why_mk_ip: 'If a final invoice is disputed, you may not be allowed to use the campaign you mostly paid for.',
    rk_why_mk_rebate: 'You cannot check whether the agency passes back the discounts it gets on advertising, so money can quietly leak.',
    rk_why_nd_inj: 'If someone leaks your secrets, money paid months later does not undo the damage; this would let you ask a court to stop the leak quickly.',
    rk_why_nd_term: 'Keeping things secret for this long is unusual, and a court may refuse to hold anyone to it.',
    rk_why_pk_ip: 'If the supplier claims your artwork or printing plates, moving to another supplier could be blocked or delayed.',
    rk_why_pk_moq: 'When your packaging design changes, nobody has agreed who pays for the old packaging left in the warehouse.',
    rk_why_ps_cap: 'What they owe you for a mistake is limited to their fee, which may be far less than a costly mistake would cost you.',
    rk_why_ps_indep: 'If the adviser has a conflict of interest they did not tell you about, their work could be useless to you.',
    rk_why_rl_listing: 'Fees and discounts are lumped together, which makes it easy for money to leak and hard to check the bills.',
    rk_why_rl_pay: 'Waiting this long to be paid ties up your cash, and the risk grows if the shop pays late.',
    rk_why_rl_return: 'It is unclear who pays when nearly out-of-date or damaged stock is sent back, so you may end up paying for it.',
    rk_why_rm_index: 'The price is checked against an unnamed market price, so every price review can turn into an argument.',
    rk_why_rm_kebs: 'Without a named quality standard it is hard to reject poor material, and it could end up in your products.',
    rk_why_rm_mat: 'The material is not described, so it is hard to say what counts as a good or a bad delivery.',
    rk_why_rm_sec: 'You rely on one supplier for a key input; if they fail, your production could stop.',
    rk_why_t_dp: 'You stay responsible for how this supplier handles people’s personal data, even though the contract says nothing about it.',
    rk_why_t_law_risk: 'Disputes would be settled under another country’s law, which is slower and more expensive for you.',
    rk_why_t_law_ambiguity: 'Disputes would be settled under your own country’s law, which keeps things close to home and predictable.',
    rk_why_t_law_missing: 'The contract does not say which country’s law applies, so where and how a dispute would be settled is unclear.',
    rk_why_t_liab: 'Contracts written by the other side often limit what they owe you when things go wrong and make you pay for their losses.',
    rk_why_t_pay_risk: 'Waiting this long to be paid ties up your cash, and the risk grows if they pay late.',
    rk_why_t_pay_ambiguity: 'The time allowed for payment looks reasonable; check it is what was agreed.',
    rk_why_t_renew: 'The contract renews by itself, so if you miss the notice date you may be stuck with it for another term.',
    rk_why_t_stamp: 'Nothing shows the tax on this lease was paid, which can make the lease hard to rely on and bring penalties.',
    rk_why_t_term: 'This is how much warning you must give to end the contract, so it sets how fast you can walk away.',
    rk_why_u_cp: 'No other party is recorded, so it is unclear who you could hold to this contract.',
    rk_why_u_law: 'If another country’s law applies, settling a dispute is slower and more expensive for you; check which country is named.',
    rk_why_u_legal: 'The other side wrote this contract, and a lawyer reading it line by line will catch things this check cannot.',
    rk_why_u_liab: 'Contracts written by the other side often limit what they owe you and make you pay for their losses, which can cost more than the deal is worth.',
    rk_why_u_noext: 'The text could not be read, so these points are a checklist, not a reading of the contract.',
    rk_why_u_ocr: 'The text was read from a scan, so dates, amounts and names may be wrong; a wrong date means a wrong renewal reminder.',
    rk_why_u_term: 'If the contract renews by itself and the notice period is long, you can get stuck with it.',
    rk_why_u_val: 'No value is recorded, so approval limits, tax and reports cannot be worked out for this contract.',
    rk_why_wh_ins: 'If the warehouse has no insurance, a fire or flood could leave you with a loss that nobody pays for.',
    rk_why_wh_temp: 'If chilled goods get too warm, nobody has agreed who pays for the spoiled stock.',
